  "metadata": {
    "tags": "Anachronistic cave-pop lament, slow lurching groove, primitive acoustic guitar with dry finger noise, hollow log percussion and stones struck in irregular machine-like patterns, flickering analog synth pulses, dial-up modem harmonies used as background texture, distant monastic choir, intimate weary lead vocal, verses sparse and claustrophobic, chorus widening into a ritual lament, stark close-miked production with abrupt dropouts and dusty tape coloration",
    "prompt": "[Verse 1]\nAll my friends are\nones and zeros,\nAnd I\u2019m one\nof the lonely ones\nSince God stopped\nListening to my\nSorrows\n\n[Verse 2]\nMy best is what I gave\nIt\u2019s all I had\nLive the rest\nOf my years\nAs a nomad\nI\u2019ll take my torch\nAnd head back to the\nCave\nCarve a status on the wall\nAnd wait for it to save\n\n[Chorus]\nAm I the one\nor the zero?\nAm I lost or just alone?\nI keep sending out a signal\nTo a world that isn\u2019t home\n\n[Post-Chorus]\nAm I the one\nor the zero?\nAm I the one\nNo one knows\n\n[Bridge]\nAll my friends are\nOnes and zeros\nOnes and zeros\nOnes and zeros\n\n[Outro]\nAnd I\u2019m one of\nthe\nlonely\nones",
